                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The first 30 minutes were inredibly boring. No people to talk to. Monsters don't respawn so could not grind experience or coins to cover potions needed.  Nearly all the doors in the town were not openable - I don't mean locked - not part of the game so why have so many doors? NO hidden resources in barrels or cupboards behind the doors that could lock. Everytime there was a battle there were at least 2 x misses on striking the foe which made the characters HP vey low and with the inability to buy more consumables the whole enjoyment was sucked out of the game. You have to use the consulmables because there was no place for the characters to rest to restor HP and MP. The battles were SLOW and I mean very SLOW. At least 10 f the 15 hours of promised game play are because of the slow battle mechanics. I did not like this game at all. Make more like Aveyond - with a believable story line, world to explore, stuff to find, puzzles to solve, This was just cheap and nasty. No diamond in the rough here,",
